    <h2>Why is Background Removal a Game-Changer?</h2>
    <p>A clean, transparent background offers incredible creative flexibility. Here are just a few reasons why this feature is so popular:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>E-commerce and Product Photography:</strong> Marketplaces like Amazon and Shopify require product photos to be on a pure white or neutral background. Removing the original background ensures a clean, consistent look across your entire product catalog, focusing the customer's attention solely on the item for sale.</li>
        <li><strong>Graphic Design:</strong> Designers constantly need to place subjects into different environments. By removing the background from a person, object, or logo, you can easily place it onto a new backdrop, a marketing banner, or a social media post.</li>
        <li><strong>Logo and Branding:</strong> A logo with a transparent background (usually saved as a PNG) can be overlaid on any color, image, or video without an ugly white box around it. This is essential for professional branding.</li>
